<title>BELGIUM: EU vets KNP BT buy of two Bunzl units.</title>
<headline>EU vets KNP BT buy of two Bunzl units.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Thursday it had started a routine review of the plans of Dutch paper and office equipment group NV Koninklijke KNP BT to take over two paper wholesalers from Britain's Bunzl Plc.</p>
<p>The units concerned are Wilhelm Seiler GmbH in Wuppertal, Germany, and Milan-based Bunzl Italia SpA.</p>
<p>Seiler has 14 outlets in Germany and Bunzl Italia has 11 centres in Italy. The two firms expect combined 1996 turnover of more than 550 million guilders and employ 500 people.</p>
<p>Under EU rules, the Commission has one month to complete its investigation. If it has doubts about the deal's impact on competition it may start a second-stage, four-month, inquiry.</p>
<p>Most deals are cleared after the initial review.</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom +32 2 287 68 11</p>
